# Breakfast of Champions — Meta Workspace

You are working in a two-repo workspace. Treat paths carefully.

## Layout

- `specs/` — OpenSpec source of truth (design, requirements, deltas)
  - `specs/canonical/` — accepted, stable specs
  - `specs/active_deltas/` — in-flight changes not yet merged into canonical
- `game-project/` — Godot game implementation (separate git repo)
  - `scenes/`, `scripts/`, `project.godot`

Open this folder (`breakfast-of-champions-meta/`) as the Cursor workspace root. Do not open `game-project/` alone unless the user asks.

## Spec-first rules

1. Specs are authoritative. Before implementing gameplay, systems, or content changes, read relevant files under `specs/canonical/` and any matching work under `specs/active_deltas/`.
2. Prefer proposing or updating an active delta over inventing behavior that contradicts canonical specs.
3. When a delta is accepted, update canonical specs and remove or archive the delta.
4. Keep implementation details in `game-project/`; keep intent, constraints, and acceptance criteria in `specs/`.

## Godot implementation rules

1. Put scenes in `game-project/scenes/` and scripts in `game-project/scripts/` unless an existing convention says otherwise.
2. Prefer small, named scripts over large god-objects.
3. Do not commit Godot editor cache (`.godot/`) or OS junk; respect `game-project/.gitignore`.
4. Meta-repo commits must not swallow the nested Godot repo. `game-project/` is independently versioned.

## Git boundaries

- Meta repo (`breakfast-of-champions-meta/`): tracks `.cursorrules`, `specs/`, and meta tooling only.
- Godot repo (`game-project/`): tracks game assets, scenes, scripts, and `project.godot`.
- Never mix commits across the two remotes in one operation. Stage and commit inside the correct `.git` root.
